{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On that night.</b> In the derash: the night of the King of the Universe. The meaning is that HaShem does not sleep but guards Israel, and He brought about the cause of the remembering of past deeds because the king's sleep fled. Some say the reason for bringing the book of chronicles was to entertain him with hearing of past events, and some say because his sleep fled — perhaps he is being punished for a vow he made and did not fulfill, and this is close to me."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:03.224143129Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}